# scripts/e2e/.env.example — every var the scripts/e2e/*.sh (and the
# manifest-showcase-driver.ts it shells out to) read. Copy to
# `scripts/e2e/.env` (gitignored) and fill in real dev-cluster values; every
# script in this folder auto-loads that file if present.
#
# Convention (matches scripts/reset/): every script auto-loads
# `scripts/e2e/.env` if present via `set -a; source .env; set +a`, which runs
# BEFORE each script's own `${VAR:-default}` fallbacks. Because that `source`
# is unconditional, `.env` assignments run LAST — so for ANY var set
# (uncommented) in `.env`, that value wins over BOTH the script's hardcoded
# default AND any value you exported in your shell beforehand (last assignment
# wins; `source` clobbers the earlier export). Consequences:
#   - To override a var that IS set in `.env`, edit `.env` (or comment the
#     line out so the script falls back to its own default). A one-off prefix
#     like `E2E_TENANT=other ./run-all.sh` does NOT take effect while
#     E2E_TENANT is set in `.env` — the sourced value overwrites it.
#   - A prefix/export override only works for vars NOT set in `.env`; there the
#     script's `${VAR:-default}` sees your exported value and no `.env` line
#     clobbers it.
#
# *** DO NOT set the *_URL / *_HOST vars below unless you actually need a
# non-default target. ***
# Each bash script reads `E2E_PROVISIONING_URL` etc. into a DIFFERENTLY
# NAMED local shell variable (e.g. `PROVISIONING_URL="${E2E_PROVISIONING_URL:-
# default}"`) — so exporting `E2E_PROVISIONING_URL` has NO effect on that
# bash script's own behavior. But `manifest-showcase-driver.ts` (invoked as
# a `bun run` subprocess by manifest-apply.sh) reads the SAME env var name
# directly via `process.env.E2E_PROVISIONING_URL ?? (E2E_RESOLVE_IP ? ... :
# ...)` — if the var is exported (even to a value that matches the script's
# own default), it WINS over the `??` fallback and disables the
# `E2E_RESOLVE_IP`-based localhost rewrite entirely, so the driver tries to
# connect to the literal `*.dev.local` hostname — which does not resolve
# outside a `--resolve`/`/etc/hosts` trick — and fails with "Unable to
# connect." This is a real regression found and fixed while centralizing
# these scripts: keep these vars commented out unless you deliberately want
# to point a stage at a non-default host.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared across all four scripts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Tenant/namespace + Knative ingress base (dev.local hostnames, OrbStack).
E2E_NAMESPACE=platform-services-dev
E2E_TENANT=acme
E2E_EMAIL=yclawd@demo.io
E2E_PASSWORD=admin123

# http-workflow.sh / connector-invoke.sh talk through api-gateway;
# manifest-apply.sh talks directly to each ksvc (no gateway route existed
# when it was written — see its header comment for why). Leave commented;
# see the DO NOT set note above.
# E2E_API_URL=http://api-gateway.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_HOST_HEADER=api-gateway.platform-services-dev.dev.local

# macOS can't resolve *.dev.local without a tunnel; --resolve pins the
# hostname to this IP (127.0.0.1 assumes a port-forward/ingress tunnel).
# Set to empty to disable the rewrite (e.g. an in-cluster runner).
E2E_RESOLVE_IP=127.0.0.1

# Poll/timeout bound (seconds). Each script has its own fallback default if
# unset; override here only if your cluster is slower than dev-fast.
E2E_POLL_TIMEOUT_S=120

# Set to 1 to skip a script's own teardown (leave created resources in place
# for manual inspection). Supported by http-workflow.sh and connector-invoke.sh.
E2E_KEEP=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# manifest-apply.sh — direct-to-ksvc URLs/hosts (no api-gateway route)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave commented; see the DO NOT set note at the top of this file.

# E2E_PROVISIONING_URL=http://provisioning-service.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_PROVISIONING_HOST=provisioning-service.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_CHANNEL_URL=http://channel-service-api.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_CHANNEL_HOST=channel-service-api.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_WORKFLOW_URL=http://workflow-service-api.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_WORKFLOW_HOST=workflow-service-api.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_AGENT_ADMIN_URL=http://agent-admin-service.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_AGENT_ADMIN_HOST=agent-admin-service.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_CONNECTOR_ADMIN_URL=http://connector-admin-api.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_CONNECTOR_ADMIN_HOST=connector-admin-api.platform-services-dev.dev.local

# Namespace CNPG tenant databases live under; used by the T09 showcase
# teardown to compute the tenant's per-namespace k8s Secret names. Derived
# as "${E2E_TENANT}-dev-ns" if unset — override only if your tenant's
# namespace doesn't follow that convention.
# E2E_TENANT_NAMESPACE=acme-dev-ns

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# manifest-showcase-driver.ts — invoked by manifest-apply.sh via `bun run`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave commented; these are read directly via process.env by the driver
# (see the DO NOT set note) and derive correctly from E2E_RESOLVE_IP already.

# E2E_GATEWAY_HOST=api-gateway.platform-services-dev.dev.local
# E2E_GATEWAY_URL=   # derived from E2E_GATEWAY_HOST + E2E_RESOLVE_IP if unset
# In-cluster health-check URL for connector-admin (svc.cluster.local, not
# dev.local — used as a plausible connector `baseUrl` config value, never
# actually invoked by the driver).
# E2E_CONNECTOR_ADMIN_BASE_URL=http://connector-admin-api.platform-services-dev.svc.cluster.local
# E2E_NONCE=   # derived (timestamp + random) if unset; set for reproducible runs

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# manifest-apply.sh / http-workflow.sh — tracking-ingester Postgres assertions
# (kubectl exec + psql; tracking-ingester-service has no public query surface
# for arbitrary event lookups by manifest name/correlation id)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

E2E_TRACKING_PG_NAMESPACE=support-services-dev
E2E_TRACKING_PG_POD=postgres-0
E2E_TRACKING_PG_USER=yoizen
E2E_TRACKING_PG_DB=yoizen

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# http-workflow.sh — pre-existing adapter + extra timeouts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# STALE-DEFAULT CAVEAT: this MUST be a real, currently-registered
# connector-admin adapter id (context=external — e.g. the `pokeapi` sample
# connector seeded from integrations/http/http-connectors/connectors/
# pokeapi.json). It is NOT manifest-created by this script. Any dev-data
# wipe (scripts/reset/reset-tenant.sh truncates connector-admin's tables
# too) deletes it, so this id WILL go stale after a reset. Re-seed with:
#   curl -X POST http://connector-admin-api.<ns>.dev.local/connectors \
#     -H "x-yoizen-tenant: ${E2E_TENANT}" -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" \
#     -d @integrations/http/http-connectors/connectors/pokeapi.json
# ...or discover it by name instead of hardcoding an id:
#   GET /connectors?name=pokeapi  (with the same tenant header)
E2E_ENDPOINT_ADAPTER_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Extra timeout knobs (seconds); defaults shown are each script's own fallback.
E2E_DISABLED_CHECK_TIMEOUT_S=120
E2E_CHAIN_TIMEOUT_S=120

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# connector-invoke.sh — no extra vars beyond the shared block above
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
